{{also|suckup|suck-up}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-suck up.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{senseid|en|absorb}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[absorb]] (fluid).
#: ''The dry soil '''sucked up''' water like a sponge.''
# {{lb|en|slang|chiefly|with "to"}} To [[adulate]] or [[flatter]] somebody excessively, generally to obtain some personal [[benefit]] or [[favour]].
#: ''Jimmy '''sucked up''' to the English teacher hoping he would get an A.''

